# bat configuration. Lives here rather than in environment variables so that
# every caller agrees -- the shell alias, MANPAGER, and any fzf preview.
#
# The theme name is the FILENAME stem, tokyonight_night -- not the <key>name</key>
# inside the file, which is "TokyoNight" and does not work here (verified against
# `bat --list-themes`). The file is the official one generated by
# folke/tokyonight.nvim, so it carries the identical
# #1a1b26 background and #c0caf5 foreground as nvim, the tmarchy bar and the
# p10k prompt.
#
# NOTE: a new host must run `bat cache --build` once. bat compiles themes into
# ~/.cache/bat, which is per-host and deliberately not in this repo. Until then
# bat falls back to its default theme rather than failing, so the symptom is
# "colours look wrong", not an error.
--theme="tokyonight_night"
--style="numbers,changes,header"
